Ladybird fires runtime.onInstalled with reason “install” the first
time an extension is loaded, and with “update” when its manifest
version changes; and it fires runtime.onStartup when the browser starts,
for the extensions already installed. WebKit decides the same way, from
the version it last saw, in WebExtensionContext::
fireRuntimeInstalledEventIfNeeded() and WebExtensionContext::
fireRuntimeStartupEventIfNeeded(). Chromium’s RuntimeEventRouter also
fires “update” whenever an unpacked extension is reloaded, even at the
same version, which Ladybird doesn’t.
